    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The name Zeb likely comes from biblical or settler influences common in nineteenth century Oklahoma place names.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/zeb_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Early growth in Zeb was influenced by the nearby Ozark and Cherokee Central Railway, which transported timber and agricultural goods.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/zeb_oklahoma"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Zeb sits at an elevation of approximately 780 feet above sea level.",
